{{main|2023 Mississippi gubernatorial election}}
[[Governor of Mississippi|Governor]] [[Tate Reeves]] was elected in [[2019 Mississippi gubernatorial election|2019]] with 51.9% of the vote and ran for re-election to a second term.<ref name = "reeves">{{cite news |url=https://www.clarionledger.com/story/news/2023/01/03/mississippi-governor-tate-reeves-files-reelection-bid-republican-2023-election/69773467007/ |title=Mississippi Republican Gov. Tate Reeves files for reelection bid |work=[[Clarion Ledger]] |date=January 3, 2023|author=Reily, Ross}}</ref>

Democrat [[Brandon Presley]], [[Mississippi Public Service Commission]]er for the Northern District, was the Democratic nominee to challenge Reeves.<ref name="presley">{{Cite web |last=Hernandez |first=Rachel |date=2023-01-12 |title=Brandon Presley joins race for Mississippi governor |url=https://www.wkrg.com/state-regional/mississippi-news/brandon-presley-joins-race-for-mississippi-governor/ |access-date=2023-01-12 |website=[[WKRG]] |language=en-US}}</ref>

Reeves won re-election.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2023-11-08 |title=Republican Gov. Tate Reeves wins re-election in Mississippi |url=https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/elections/mississippi-gov-tate-reeves-wins-re-election-extending-republicans-two-rcna122075 |access-date=2023-12-12 |website=NBC News |language=en}}</ref> 

